articles=old['posts'] + [
('business-website-checklist','A practical checklist before building a business website','Define audience, content and ownership before design begins.',[
'Write down the most important visitor task first. A buyer may need to compare services, see examples, check availability or contact someone. If the task is unclear, visual choices will be harder to judge.','List the pages that support that task. Most small business sites need a focused home page, service information, credible background and contact details. Add more pages when each one answers a distinct question.','Gather real material early: service details, location, team information, images you own, testimonials you can verify, and questions customers regularly ask. Good content gives the design something useful to organize.','Decide who will update the site, how changes are approved, and who owns the domain, hosting and source. These operational details are part of a successful launch.']),
('choosing-a-website-platform','How to choose a platform for your website','A platform decision should follow publishing and maintenance needs.',[
'Start with the people who will edit the site. If a team publishes articles or changes service details often, a content management system may save time. If the site is a focused tool, a custom interface may be more appropriate.','Ask what features are essential now. Forms, payments, product catalogs and account systems each introduce ongoing work. Avoid selecting a platform only because one feature may be useful someday.','Think beyond launch. Updates, backups, hosting costs and the skills available to the owner all affect the real cost of a site.','Build a short comparison using editing workflow, required integrations, performance needs and maintenance capacity. The simplest solution that handles those needs is usually the strongest starting point.']),
('landing-page-structure','A landing page structure that helps visitors decide','Build the page around a single offer and the questions it creates.',[
'The opening screen should tell the right visitor what is offered and what to do next. A vague slogan makes people work harder to understand whether the page is for them.','Follow with the information needed to decide: what is included, who it is for, examples of the result, process and common questions. Put the strongest proof close to the claims it supports.','Use one main action consistently. The page can repeat the action after meaningful sections, but it should not introduce competing goals at every turn.','Check the page on a phone, where reading space is limited. Keep forms short, labels visible and buttons easy to tap. Measure completed enquiries rather than clicks alone.']),
('wordpress-maintenance-guide','What WordPress maintenance actually involves','Updates, backups and routine checks that keep a site useful.',[
'WordPress sites rely on a theme, plugins and hosting that change over time. Maintenance begins by knowing what is installed and which pieces the site really needs.','Take backups before significant updates and ensure there is a realistic way to restore the site. Update components in a controlled order, then check key pages, forms and purchase paths.','Review performance and broken links periodically. A page can remain online while important content or a contact form quietly stops working.','Assign ownership. Someone should know who can access the site, who approves changes and where to report an issue. A maintenance plan is useful only when it fits the site’s actual workflow.']),
('project-case-study-guide','How to write a useful website case study','Explain the problem, your decisions and the result honestly.',[
'A good case study starts with context. Who was the audience, what did they need and what limited the project? This makes design choices easier to understand.','Show the important decisions: navigation, content structure, interaction or technical approach. Screenshots are helpful when they demonstrate a specific improvement.','Separate observed results from goals. If analytics are unavailable, describe what shipped and what can be tested next instead of inventing a conversion lift.','Finish with the lessons that might help a similar project. A concise, honest account is more useful than a long list of technologies.']),
('mobile-first-design-checklist','Mobile-first design checks for a business website','Practical checks for navigation, reading and enquiry flows.',[
'Mobile design starts with the most important visitor task. Make the offer, navigation and action visible without requiring precision taps or long scanning.','Test real content at narrow widths. Long headings, tables, forms and cards often expose layout issues that empty placeholders hide.','Check that text can grow, interactive elements have enough space, and the page does not scroll sideways. Consider slow connections and older devices as part of the experience.','Review the full enquiry journey on a phone. A fast home page does little good if the contact step is confusing or the final action opens the wrong destination.']),
('sitemap-and-robots','What robots.txt and a sitemap actually do','Understand crawl guidance without treating it as a ranking shortcut.',[
'A robots.txt file gives crawler instructions about where it may access content. It is not a way to make private information secure; protected data needs proper access controls.','An XML sitemap lists canonical URLs you want crawlers to discover. Keep it current and leave out duplicates, redirects and pages that should not be indexed.','Neither file guarantees indexing or ranking. Search engines also assess page quality, technical accessibility and whether the content answers a real need.','After launch, inspect the sitemap and important URLs in Search Console when available. Fix crawl errors and focus on useful content before adding more pages.']),
('website-redesign-plan','How to plan a website redesign without losing useful pages','Audit content and URLs before changing the visual system.',[
'Begin with a page inventory. Record which URLs exist, what each page is for and which pages bring visitors or enquiries. A redesign can accidentally remove the very content people use.','Interview the people who maintain the site and those who answer enquiries. Their recurring questions reveal where the current structure is confusing.','Prototype the most important route first, then apply the visual system to the other pages. Preserve or redirect URLs deliberately when their content changes.','After launch, verify navigation, forms, redirects, metadata and analytics. Monitor actual search and enquiry data for issues the design review did not reveal.'])]
project_notes={
'hushly':('A personal link is the entry point, so the page has to make the recipient and the next action immediately clear. After submission, the account owner needs a readable inbox and a reliable path to reply.','This kind of product lives in shared social links. I pay particular attention to narrow screens, signup friction, message states and the language around privacy.'),
'jabalpur-connect':('A local community product needs more than a profile card. Discovery, preferences, mutual interest, chat and account controls have to form a coherent path.','For a social experience, clear reporting and blocking routes are part of the interface. I also consider how visitors understand what is public on a profile and what stays inside a conversation.'),
'happyhealing':('A storefront is both a catalog and an introduction to the brand. Product organization, readable descriptions and a clear buying path help visitors decide with confidence.','Handloom products benefit from context: fabric, craft, care and imagery. Those details give the page substance beyond a generic product grid.'),
'john-stamang':('A consulting site must explain who the service helps and what a prospective client can expect. The navigation should lead from the offer to examples and contact.','For specialist work, clarity is a design asset. Simple typography and carefully grouped service information can make the expertise easier to understand.'),
'fitcoach':('A fitness offer needs a strong opening promise grounded in the actual service, then a simple route into plans or enquiry.','Mobile visitors often arrive from a short link. The page therefore needs a short visual path, readable sections and one clear next action.'),
'flipbook-converter':('The conversion task should lead the page: choose a document, understand the expected format and see what happens next.','A utility needs explicit progress, success and error states. File limitations and output expectations should be visible before a user commits time to uploading.'),
'invoice-generator':('Invoice tools are used for a task with little patience for unnecessary setup. Labels, calculations and preview need to stay close together.','A useful export flow should preserve the entered information, show the final document clearly and make the download action easy to find.'),
'resume-builder':('A resume builder has to help people choose what to include, not just decorate the final page.','Live preview can make formatting decisions easier, but the entered information should remain readable and easy to edit at each step.'),
'college-management':('Academic administration spans people with different jobs. Student information, attendance, fees and notices should be grouped by task.','Permission and data handling become important in a real deployment. This project is presented as an interface concept; production use would need careful requirements and access design.'),
'multi-tool-hub':('A collection of utilities works when each task is easy to find and fast to start. The index is part of the product.','Tool pages should use consistent labels and interaction patterns while still explaining their particular input and output.'),
'shri-dadaji':('A local shop needs visitors to find its location, product categories and a real way to get in touch.','The content should speak to the farmers it serves and make the inventory understandable without claiming online stock that may change.'),
'dhanda-tycoon':('The first screen of an interactive project should show visitors what they can do and what changes when they act.','Clear feedback after each decision makes experimentation more satisfying.'),
'life-meter':('A reflective experience should make its framing understandable before asking visitors for information.','Sensitive personal inputs deserve plain language and a clear explanation of how they are handled.'),
'weight-loss-calendar':('A calendar view can turn an abstract goal into a sequence of manageable days.','The interface should support consistent tracking without making health promises.'),
'zen-flow-henna':('Visual craft benefits from generous space and a clear path from examples to an enquiry.','The gallery and service details should reflect real work and remain usable on phones.')}
